Committee Secretary: For the GSIS, we have President and General Manager Jose Arnulfo Veloso and EVP Jason Teng. We have also invited representatives from DBM and COA.

asr-000097
00:43:18.360 --> 00:43:21.860
Committee Secretary: From DBM, we have Ms. Mercedes de la Cruz, Ms. Aileen Malit.

asr-000098
00:43:22.160 --> 00:43:24.300
Committee Secretary: Ms. Faith Quintero and Ms. Hannah Navarro.

asr-000099
00:43:24.300 --> 00:43:48.540
Committee Secretary: For COA, we have Attorney Isabel Sirenia, Ms. Wilma Gismundo, Ms. Marian Catalan, Ms. Nicole Trinidad, Ms. Applejoy Doctolero, Ms. Paula Wilma Candelaria, Mr. Lester Bitangor, Ms. Catherine Mones, Ms. Yelan Castillo, Mr. Noriel Legrimas, Ms. Andrea Marie Alavastro, Mr. John Victor Valle, Mr. Mark Zenin Hipolito, and Ms. Monique Angelique Carvajal.

asr-000100
00:43:48.660 --> 00:43:49.480
Committee Secretary: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000101
00:43:50.220 --> 00:43:51.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, ComSec.

asr-000102
00:43:52.160 --> 00:43:58.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The Chair would like to acknowledge the presence of Senator Francis Pangilina. Thank you, sir, for joining us.

asr-000103
00:43:59.020 --> 00:43:59.500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you.

asr-000104
00:44:01.760 --> 00:44:09.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Now, the Chair would like to give his opening statement. Good afternoon to our colleagues here at the Senate, guests, and resource persons, and to the Department of Finance.

asr-000105
00:44:09.900 --> 00:44:19.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Today, the Committee on Finance will deliberate the proposed budget of the DOF, its attached agencies, and cooperation for the fiscal year 2027,

asr-000106
00:44:19.740 --> 00:44:22.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and discuss relevant points in strengthening our economy.

asr-000109
00:44:22.320 --> 00:44:27.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Our revenue efforts, managing debt levels, and expanding our financial resources.

asr-000110
00:44:28.560 --> 00:44:36.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The Department of Finance plays a critical role in ensuring that the government has sufficient resources to fund our priorities,

asr-000111
00:44:36.900 --> 00:44:44.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: from healthcare and education to infrastructure, agriculture, social protection, and other essential services.

asr-000112
00:44:45.140 --> 00:44:48.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: To fund government programs and projects, revenue collection is critical.

asr-000114
00:44:49.360 --> 00:44:52.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kailangan nating malaman ang improvement sa

asr-000115
00:44:52.160 --> 00:44:59.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: BIR tax administration, digitalization at enforcement ay talagang nagresulta sa mas mataas na koleksyon,

asr-000116
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:03.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: mas maayos na compliance at mas kaunting tax leakages.

asr-000117
00:45:04.860 --> 00:45:09.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: On the other hand, Bureau of Customs continues to face persistent challenges

asr-000118
00:45:09.300 --> 00:45:12.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: in combating smuggling and illicit trade.

asr-000119
00:45:12.300 --> 00:45:17.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya nais nating malaman sa kabila ng mas mababang budget ngayong taon,

asr-000120
00:45:17.680 --> 00:45:19.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: kaya ba nating palakasin ang border protection,

asr-000121
00:45:20.540 --> 00:45:23.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: masugpo ang smuggling at mapataas ang revenue collection.

asr-000122
00:45:23.420 --> 00:45:30.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As the government continues to operate within a challenging fiscal environment

asr-000123
00:45:30.300 --> 00:45:35.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and as we seek additional revenues, equally important are sound debt management,

asr-000124
00:45:36.500 --> 00:45:38.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: responsible borrowing, and prudent spending.

asr-000125
00:45:39.540 --> 00:45:45.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So in discussing the proposed budget today, we want clear answers on three basic questions.

asr-000126
00:45:46.080 --> 00:45:48.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tama at sapat ba ang ating kinukulekta?

asr-000127
00:45:49.180 --> 00:45:52.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Maayos at efficient ba nating ginagamit ang bawat piso?

asr-000128
00:45:52.660 --> 00:45:58.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At responsable ba nating pinamamahalan ang ating utang at fiscal obligations

asr-000129
00:45:58.480 --> 00:46:01.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: upang hindi nating ipasa sa susunod na henerasyon?

asr-000130
00:46:02.940 --> 00:46:05.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As our economy and fiscal needs continue to evolve,

asr-000131
00:46:05.860 --> 00:46:10.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: we must ensure that our country remains in a stable and sustainable fiscal position.

asr-000132
00:46:11.740 --> 00:46:15.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And we owe it to the Filipino taxpayers to ensure that every peso requested

asr-000133
00:46:15.780 --> 00:46:18.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: is a peso efficiently and responsibly spent.

asr-000134
00:46:19.240 --> 00:46:20.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Today's hearing gives us an opportunity

asr-000135
00:46:20.940 --> 00:46:22.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to examine whether we can achieve a sustainable future

asr-000136
00:46:22.640 --> 00:46:26.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and whether our revenue strategies, borrowings, investments,

asr-000137
00:46:27.200 --> 00:46:30.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and financing mechanisms are putting us on the right track,

asr-000138
00:46:31.080 --> 00:46:33.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: not only for the coming year but for the years ahead.

asr-000139
00:46:34.680 --> 00:46:35.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you very much.

asr-000140
00:46:36.540 --> 00:46:40.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And welcome, Secretary Frederick Go, the Undersecretaries,

asr-000141
00:46:41.060 --> 00:46:47.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Treasurer Sharon Almanza, the USECs, ASECs, and the heads of agencies.

asr-000142
00:46:47.760 --> 00:46:50.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Welcome to the DOF budget briefing.

asr-000143
00:46:50.540 --> 00:46:50.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-000144
00:46:51.560 --> 00:46:52.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I have worked with a lot of people.

asr-000145
00:46:52.640 --> 00:46:54.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Some of you, familiar faces.

asr-000146
00:46:54.800 --> 00:46:56.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We have passed a lot of vital measures.

asr-000147
00:46:58.280 --> 00:46:59.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pinagod niyo ako.

asr-000148
00:47:00.320 --> 00:47:03.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ilang measures yun, mga technical, but through your help.

asr-000149
00:47:03.840 --> 00:47:05.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung si Carlo, yung si Catherine Fong.

asr-000150
00:47:06.560 --> 00:47:11.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: These are the people that backstop, that make me look good.

asr-000151
00:47:11.880 --> 00:47:16.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kahit nahirap at technical yung mga pinagpapasako, salamat sa inyo.

asr-000152
00:47:17.200 --> 00:47:21.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Anyway, I'd like to ask Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan

asr-000153
00:47:21.700 --> 00:47:22.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: for his opinion.

asr-000154
00:47:22.640 --> 00:47:24.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: His opening statements, if there's any.

asr-000155
00:47:25.120 --> 00:47:29.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I would rather listen to their presentations, Mr. Chairperson.

asr-000156
00:47:29.020 --> 00:47:30.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, since there are no more questions,

asr-000157
00:47:30.820 --> 00:47:34.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I now call on Secretary Frederick Go to deliver his opening statement

asr-000158
00:47:34.240 --> 00:47:38.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and to present the 2027 proposed expenditure program

asr-000159
00:47:38.060 --> 00:47:40.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: of the Department of Finance and its attached agencies and corporations.

asr-000160
00:47:41.760 --> 00:47:42.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The floor, sir.

asr-000161
00:47:43.520 --> 00:47:47.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Thank you, Chairperson Senator JV Ejercito,

asr-000162
00:47:47.520 --> 00:47:50.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Vice Chairperson, Senator Kiko Pangilinan,

asr-000163
00:47:51.280 --> 00:47:52.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Senate Committee Member,

asr-000164
00:47:52.640 --> 00:47:54.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: members, colleagues in government, good afternoon.

asr-000165
00:47:55.060 --> 00:47:57.960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Thank you for this opportunity to present the proposed

asr-000166
00:47:57.960 --> 00:48:02.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: fiscal year 2027 budget of the Department of Finance,

asr-000167
00:48:02.760 --> 00:48:05.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: its bureaus, and attached agencies.

asr-000168
00:48:06.020 --> 00:48:07.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The DOF has a critical mandate,

asr-000169
00:48:08.420 --> 00:48:10.280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: raise resources the government needs,

asr-000170
00:48:11.080 --> 00:48:12.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: manage them responsibly,

asr-000171
00:48:13.060 --> 00:48:15.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and protect the country's fiscal stability.

asr-000172
00:48:16.000 --> 00:48:18.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We are the government's fundraiser,

asr-000173
00:48:18.660 --> 00:48:21.820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: but raising revenue is only one part of the job.

asr-000174
00:48:22.640 --> 00:48:24.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We also have to manage debt,

asr-000175
00:48:24.820 --> 00:48:26.480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: strengthen financial systems,

asr-000176
00:48:27.300 --> 00:48:29.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: improve tax and customs administration,

asr-000177
00:48:29.840 --> 00:48:32.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and make sure that the government has the fiscal space

asr-000178
00:48:32.540 --> 00:48:33.980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to fund its priorities.

asr-000179
00:48:36.260 --> 00:48:39.280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: When this administration took office in 2022,

asr-000180
00:48:39.460 --> 00:48:42.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the country was carrying 12.79 trillion

asr-000181
00:48:42.200 --> 00:48:44.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in national government debt,

asr-000182
00:48:45.200 --> 00:48:47.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: much of it accumulated during the pandemic.

asr-000183
00:48:48.200 --> 00:48:50.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our task since then has been clear,

asr-000184
00:48:51.320 --> 00:48:52.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: rebuild fiscal space,

asr-000185
00:48:52.640 --> 00:48:54.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while continuing to support growth

asr-000186
00:48:54.520 --> 00:48:56.300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and invest in the country's future.

asr-000187
00:48:57.520 --> 00:48:58.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As a response,

asr-000188
00:48:58.500 --> 00:49:02.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we crafted the country's medium-term fiscal framework in 2022,

asr-000189
00:49:02.920 --> 00:49:05.900
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the government's blueprint for reducing our deficit and debt

asr-000190
00:49:05.900 --> 00:49:07.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: as a percentage of GDP,

asr-000191
00:49:08.460 --> 00:49:09.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while creating more jobs,

asr-000192
00:49:10.020 --> 00:49:11.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: increasing people's incomes,

asr-000193
00:49:11.940 --> 00:49:13.480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and reducing poverty.

asr-000194
00:49:14.200 --> 00:49:18.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It set us on a path of gradual and sustained fiscal consolidation

asr-000195
00:49:18.560 --> 00:49:20.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to restore fiscal space,

asr-000196
00:49:20.860 --> 00:49:22.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while continuing to invest in the future,

asr-000197
00:49:22.620 --> 00:49:24.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while continuing to invest in the foundations of growth.

asr-000198
00:49:25.100 --> 00:49:28.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But our recovery has not happened in an easy environment.

asr-000199
00:49:29.840 --> 00:49:30.480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Over the years,

asr-000200
00:49:30.580 --> 00:49:32.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: external pressures and global uncertainties

asr-000201
00:49:32.780 --> 00:49:34.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: have disrupted supply chains

asr-000202
00:49:34.460 --> 00:49:36.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and pushed inflation up,

asr-000203
00:49:36.740 --> 00:49:38.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: affecting the pace of growth.

asr-000204
00:49:39.120 --> 00:49:40.300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In this context,

asr-000205
00:49:40.440 --> 00:49:43.300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we needed to recalibrate our growth and fiscal targets

asr-000206
00:49:43.300 --> 00:49:45.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to keep them realistic and responsive

asr-000207
00:49:45.460 --> 00:49:47.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to evolving economic conditions.

asr-000208
00:49:47.980 --> 00:49:50.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But the direction of our fiscal policy

asr-000209
00:49:50.460 --> 00:49:51.660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: has remained consistent.

asr-000210
00:49:51.900 --> 00:49:52.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We have been working hard to ensure that

asr-000211
00:49:52.600 --> 00:49:54.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have pursued stronger revenue collection,

asr-000212
00:49:55.240 --> 00:49:56.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: disciplined expenditure,

asr-000213
00:49:57.020 --> 00:49:58.960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and prudent debt management.

asr-000214
00:50:00.280 --> 00:50:05.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Total revenues have grown by an average of 10.54% annually

asr-000215
00:50:05.360 --> 00:50:07.980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: over the last four years.

asr-000216
00:50:09.080 --> 00:50:10.740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And in 2025,

asr-000217
00:50:11.040 --> 00:50:13.940
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the BIR surpassed 3 trillion pesos

asr-000218
00:50:13.940 --> 00:50:16.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in tax collections for the first time.

asr-000219
00:50:17.080 --> 00:50:19.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We continue to strengthen collections

asr-000220
00:50:19.240 --> 00:50:21.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while mobilizing additional non-tax revenues

asr-000221
00:50:21.800 --> 00:50:22.580
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and managing the economy.

asr-000222
00:50:22.600 --> 00:50:26.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As a result,

asr-000223
00:50:26.820 --> 00:50:29.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the fiscal deficit has continued to narrow

asr-000224
00:50:29.120 --> 00:50:31.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: as we remain on track

asr-000225
00:50:31.180 --> 00:50:34.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: toward our medium-term consolidation targets.

asr-000226
00:50:35.100 --> 00:50:37.300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: From 8.6% in 2021

asr-000227
00:50:37.300 --> 00:50:39.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and 7.3% in 2022,

asr-000228
00:50:40.240 --> 00:50:43.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we are bringing it down to 5.4%

asr-000229
00:50:43.100 --> 00:50:45.300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: by the end of 2026.

asr-000230
00:50:47.280 --> 00:50:50.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our debt indicators also remain manageable.

asr-000231
00:50:50.440 --> 00:50:51.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In 2025,

asr-000232
00:50:51.700 --> 00:50:55.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: national government debt stood at 63.2% of GDP

asr-000233
00:50:55.700 --> 00:51:00.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while general government debt settled at 56.8% of GDP,

asr-000234
00:51:01.060 --> 00:51:04.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: well below the 70% international benchmark

asr-000235
00:51:04.080 --> 00:51:05.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for debt sustainability

asr-000236
00:51:05.640 --> 00:51:08.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and within a manageable range

asr-000237
00:51:08.260 --> 00:51:11.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: compared with other emerging economies.

asr-000238
00:51:11.680 --> 00:51:13.060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: More importantly,

asr-000239
00:51:13.440 --> 00:51:16.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have maintained a prudent debt mix,

asr-000240
00:51:16.780 --> 00:51:17.920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: predominantly domestic,

asr-000241
00:51:18.280 --> 00:51:20.300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: predominantly carrying fixed interest rates,

asr-000242
00:51:20.300 --> 00:51:21.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and predominantly,

asr-000243
00:51:21.700 --> 00:51:24.480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: structured with long repayment terms

asr-000244
00:51:24.480 --> 00:51:27.580
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of at least five years.

asr-000245
00:51:28.540 --> 00:51:28.920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: First,

asr-000246
00:51:29.500 --> 00:51:33.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 67% of our debt is domestic.

asr-000247
00:51:33.700 --> 00:51:36.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This reduces our exposure to foreign exchange risks

asr-000248
00:51:36.620 --> 00:51:39.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while also supporting the continued development

asr-000249
00:51:39.400 --> 00:51:41.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our local capital market.

asr-000250
00:51:41.980 --> 00:51:42.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Second,

asr-000251
00:51:42.780 --> 00:51:45.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 90% of our debt carries fixed interest rates.

asr-000252
00:51:46.020 --> 00:51:47.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This provides greater certainty

asr-000253
00:51:47.520 --> 00:51:48.980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in our debt servicing costs

asr-000254
00:51:48.980 --> 00:51:51.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and shields us from sudden increases

asr-000255
00:51:51.140 --> 00:51:51.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or fluctuations

asr-000256
00:51:51.700 --> 00:51:53.340
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in global interest rates.

asr-000257
00:51:54.380 --> 00:51:55.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And third,

asr-000258
00:51:55.580 --> 00:51:57.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 84.1% of our debt

asr-000259
00:51:57.860 --> 00:52:00.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: has long-term repayment periods,

asr-000260
00:52:00.560 --> 00:52:01.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: meaning we have several years

asr-000261
00:52:01.780 --> 00:52:03.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: before these obligations fall due.

asr-000262
00:52:05.440 --> 00:52:07.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: These generally refer to debt

asr-000263
00:52:07.880 --> 00:52:10.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: with maturities of over five years.

asr-000264
00:52:11.520 --> 00:52:13.740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This longer maturity profile

asr-000265
00:52:13.740 --> 00:52:15.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: reduces our refinancing risks

asr-000266
00:52:15.720 --> 00:52:17.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and gives us greater predictability

asr-000267
00:52:17.780 --> 00:52:19.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in managing our debt obligations.

asr-000268
00:52:20.460 --> 00:52:21.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This strategic,

asr-000269
00:52:21.700 --> 00:52:22.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: borrowing mix

asr-000270
00:52:22.640 --> 00:52:24.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: strengthened our resilience

asr-000271
00:52:24.240 --> 00:52:25.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to external shocks

asr-000272
00:52:25.260 --> 00:52:27.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and made our debt obligations

asr-000273
00:52:27.120 --> 00:52:27.840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: more predictable

asr-000274
00:52:27.840 --> 00:52:28.660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and manageable

asr-000275
00:52:28.660 --> 00:52:30.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: over the long term.

asr-000276
00:52:31.940 --> 00:52:33.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The market's assessment

asr-000277
00:52:33.860 --> 00:52:35.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our fiscal fundamentals

asr-000278
00:52:35.400 --> 00:52:36.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is also reflected

asr-000279
00:52:36.420 --> 00:52:37.320
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the confidence

asr-000280
00:52:37.320 --> 00:52:39.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of international investors.

asr-000281
00:52:39.880 --> 00:52:41.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our sovereign credit ratings

asr-000282
00:52:41.360 --> 00:52:43.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: remain at investment-grade levels.

asr-000283
00:52:44.220 --> 00:52:46.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We have two A- ratings

asr-000284
00:52:46.040 --> 00:52:48.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from Japanese credit rating agencies,

asr-000285
00:52:48.540 --> 00:52:49.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and this reflects

asr-000286
00:52:49.780 --> 00:52:50.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: continued confidence

asr-000287
00:52:50.780 --> 00:52:51.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the country's

asr-000288
00:52:51.680 --> 00:52:53.060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: economic fundamentals

asr-000289
00:52:53.060 --> 00:52:54.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and our capacity

asr-000290
00:52:54.500 --> 00:52:57.300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to manage our public finances.

asr-000291
00:52:58.720 --> 00:53:00.940
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Higher credit ratings reflect

asr-000292
00:53:00.940 --> 00:53:02.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: minimal default risk,

asr-000293
00:53:02.600 --> 00:53:04.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: signaling lenders

asr-000294
00:53:04.240 --> 00:53:06.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to offer lower interest rates.

asr-000295
00:53:06.680 --> 00:53:07.840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: When the country can borrow

asr-000296
00:53:07.840 --> 00:53:08.920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at lower interest rates,

asr-000297
00:53:08.920 --> 00:53:10.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: private businesses can also borrow

asr-000298
00:53:10.800 --> 00:53:12.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at lower interest rates.

asr-000299
00:53:13.840 --> 00:53:15.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We have also seen progress

asr-000300
00:53:15.080 --> 00:53:15.960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in our integration

asr-000301
00:53:15.960 --> 00:53:17.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: into global capital markets

asr-000302
00:53:17.420 --> 00:53:19.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: with the upcoming historic debut

asr-000303
00:53:19.720 --> 00:53:21.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our peso-denominated government bonds in

asr-000304
00:53:21.620 --> 00:53:24.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: JPMorgan's Government Bond Index

asr-000305
00:53:24.620 --> 00:53:25.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Emerging Markets

asr-000306
00:53:25.620 --> 00:53:28.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in January 2027.

asr-000307
00:53:28.700 --> 00:53:30.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This is significant

asr-000308
00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:31.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: because our first-ever inclusion

asr-000309
00:53:31.880 --> 00:53:34.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in a major global bond index

asr-000310
00:53:34.520 --> 00:53:36.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: reflects a strong vote of confidence

asr-000311
00:53:36.440 --> 00:53:37.940
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in our solid fundamentals

asr-000312
00:53:37.940 --> 00:53:40.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and fiscal discipline.

asr-000313
00:53:40.580 --> 00:53:42.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: These results are the product

asr-000314
00:53:42.120 --> 00:53:43.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of disciplined fiscal management,

asr-000315
00:53:44.340 --> 00:53:46.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and the 2027 proposed budget

asr-000316
00:53:46.500 --> 00:53:49.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: carries that same discipline forward.

asr-000317
00:53:49.780 --> 00:53:51.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: For next year,

asr-000318
00:53:51.020 --> 00:53:54.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our new general appropriations

asr-000319
00:53:54.420 --> 00:53:58.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: amount to 28.6 billion pesos.

asr-000320
00:53:58.260 --> 00:54:00.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Automatic appropriations

asr-000321
00:54:00.260 --> 00:54:02.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: will be 3.4 billion pesos,

asr-000322
00:54:02.180 --> 00:54:03.740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: including retirement

asr-000323
00:54:03.740 --> 00:54:05.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and life insurance premiums

asr-000324
00:54:05.220 --> 00:54:06.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and special accounts

asr-000325
00:54:06.260 --> 00:54:07.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the general fund.

asr-000326
00:54:07.260 --> 00:54:10.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Overall, we have a department-wide allocation

asr-000327
00:54:10.520 --> 00:54:13.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of 32.034 billion pesos,

asr-000328
00:54:13.220 --> 00:54:16.300
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which is 3.49% lower

asr-000329
00:54:16.300 --> 00:54:19.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: than the 2026 GAA level,

asr-000330
00:54:19.140 --> 00:54:21.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: equivalent to a decrease

asr-000331
00:54:21.020 --> 00:54:24.900
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of 1.159 billion pesos.

asr-000332
00:54:25.480 --> 00:54:26.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Against a government

asr-000333
00:54:26.460 --> 00:54:29.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that must raise trillions of pesos

asr-000334
00:54:29.020 --> 00:54:29.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in revenue

asr-000335
00:54:29.700 --> 00:54:31.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and finance trillions more

asr-000336
00:54:31.880 --> 00:54:33.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in public expenditure,

asr-000337
00:54:33.920 --> 00:54:35.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the DOF and its attached agencies

asr-000338
00:54:35.860 --> 00:54:39.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: operate on a relatively small budget

asr-000339
00:54:39.220 --> 00:54:41.900
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at 19.4 billion pesos.

asr-000340
00:54:42.540 --> 00:54:44.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This accounts for more than half

asr-000341
00:54:44.000 --> 00:54:46.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or about 61% of the total

asr-000342
00:54:46.100 --> 00:54:48.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: DOF proposed budget.

asr-000343
00:54:49.180 --> 00:54:50.740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Against this budget,

asr-000344
00:54:50.740 --> 00:54:52.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the BIR is expected to collect

asr-000345
00:54:52.420 --> 00:54:56.340
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: approximately 3.7 trillion pesos

asr-000346
00:54:56.340 --> 00:54:58.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in 2027.

asr-000347
00:54:58.520 --> 00:55:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In other words,

asr-000348
00:55:00.080 --> 00:55:02.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the BIR's entire proposed budget

asr-000349
00:55:02.160 --> 00:55:04.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is equivalent to two days

asr-000350
00:55:04.560 --> 00:55:06.900
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of projected collections.

asr-000351
00:55:06.900 --> 00:55:09.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The Bureau of Customs or the BOC,

asr-000352
00:55:09.220 --> 00:55:10.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: on the other hand,

asr-000353
00:55:10.020 --> 00:55:11.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: has a proposed budget

asr-000354
00:55:11.000 --> 00:55:12.580
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of 5.9 billion pesos

asr-000355
00:55:12.580 --> 00:55:14.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: against projected collections

asr-000356
00:55:14.100 --> 00:55:18.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of approximately 1.1 trillion pesos.

asr-000357
00:55:18.560 --> 00:55:20.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Its proposed budget is likewise

asr-000358
00:55:20.420 --> 00:55:21.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: equivalent to about

asr-000359
00:55:21.720 --> 00:55:23.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: two days of collections.

asr-000360
00:55:24.620 --> 00:55:26.840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The Bureau of Treasury or the BTR

asr-000361
00:55:26.840 --> 00:55:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: has a proposed allocation

asr-000362
00:55:28.080 --> 00:55:29.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of 4.1 billion pesos.

asr-000363
00:55:30.620 --> 00:55:32.840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Its responsibility is to manage

asr-000364
00:55:32.840 --> 00:55:33.920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the government's cash,

asr-000365
00:55:34.300 --> 00:55:36.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: debt, and financing requirements,

asr-000366
00:55:36.620 --> 00:55:37.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: including the funding

asr-000367
00:55:37.620 --> 00:55:39.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of the projected

asr-000368
00:55:39.440 --> 00:55:42.280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 1.7 trillion pesos

asr-000369
00:55:42.280 --> 00:55:45.060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: fiscal deficit in 2027.

asr-000370
00:55:46.000 --> 00:55:47.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In terms of allocation,

asr-000371
00:55:47.800 --> 00:55:49.940
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: about 52% of our proposed budget

asr-000372
00:55:49.940 --> 00:55:50.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: under the new government is

asr-000373
00:55:50.200 --> 00:55:51.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: under the new general

asr-000374
00:55:51.440 --> 00:55:53.480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and automatic appropriations

asr-000375
00:55:53.480 --> 00:55:56.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: goes to personal services,

asr-000376
00:55:56.180 --> 00:55:57.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 35% to maintenance

asr-000377
00:55:57.700 --> 00:55:59.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and other operating expenses,

asr-000378
00:55:59.440 --> 00:56:02.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and about 13% to capital outlays,

asr-000379
00:56:02.720 --> 00:56:07.480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and less than 1% to financial expenses.

asr-000380
00:56:07.480 --> 00:56:09.320
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This allocation reflects our focus

asr-000381
00:56:09.320 --> 00:56:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: on workforce upskilling

asr-000382
00:56:11.080 --> 00:56:13.820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and digital infrastructure.

asr-000383
00:56:13.820 --> 00:56:15.760
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Digitalization and modernization

asr-000384
00:56:15.760 --> 00:56:18.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: initiatives remain a high priority

asr-000385
00:56:18.000 --> 00:56:19.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: across all agencies

asr-000386
00:56:19.200 --> 00:56:20.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: with a total budget

asr-000387
00:56:20.160 --> 00:56:21.660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of 3.8 billion pesos

asr-000388
00:56:21.660 --> 00:56:23.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to transform processes,

asr-000389
00:56:23.680 --> 00:56:24.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: integrate systems,

asr-000390
00:56:24.700 --> 00:56:25.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and deliver faster,

asr-000391
00:56:26.160 --> 00:56:27.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: more efficient services.

asr-000392
00:56:28.440 --> 00:56:30.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: At about 66%,

asr-000393
00:56:30.780 --> 00:56:33.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the BIR accounts

asr-000394
00:56:33.180 --> 00:56:34.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for the largest piece of the pie,

asr-000395
00:56:34.800 --> 00:56:36.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: followed by the Bureau of Customs

asr-000396
00:56:36.160 --> 00:56:37.960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at about 15%.

asr-000397
00:56:37.960 --> 00:56:39.740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: These investments are designed

asr-000398
00:56:39.740 --> 00:56:40.920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to make compliance easier

asr-000399
00:56:40.920 --> 00:56:41.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for taxpayers,

asr-000400
00:56:42.040 --> 00:56:42.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: cut red tape,

asr-000401
00:56:43.180 --> 00:56:44.340
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and foster a culture

asr-000402
00:56:44.340 --> 00:56:45.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of transparency

asr-000403
00:56:45.440 --> 00:56:47.920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in line with the President's call

asr-000404
00:56:47.920 --> 00:56:49.920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for zero tolerance on

asr-000405
00:56:50.160 --> 00:56:50.660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Corruption.

asr-000406
00:56:51.840 --> 00:56:53.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Now, allow me to present

asr-000407
00:56:53.700 --> 00:56:55.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the specific budget proposals

asr-000408
00:56:55.220 --> 00:56:56.740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of each DOF agency.

asr-000409
00:56:57.580 --> 00:56:58.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As mentioned,

asr-000410
00:56:58.640 --> 00:57:00.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the BIR has a proposed budget

asr-000411
00:57:00.020 --> 00:57:01.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of 19.4 billion pesos,

asr-000412
00:57:01.840 --> 00:57:03.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which is 6.9% higher

asr-000413
00:57:03.460 --> 00:57:04.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: than this year's GAA.

asr-000414
00:57:05.440 --> 00:57:06.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This increase is driven in part

asr-000415
00:57:06.860 --> 00:57:08.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: by higher personnel services,

asr-000416
00:57:09.040 --> 00:57:10.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: following the compensation adjustments

asr-000417
00:57:10.700 --> 00:57:12.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: under EO64,

asr-000418
00:57:12.400 --> 00:57:13.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Series of 2024.

asr-000419
00:57:14.240 --> 00:57:14.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Meanwhile,

asr-000420
00:57:14.880 --> 00:57:17.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: MOOE will grow by 22.9%

asr-000421
00:57:17.200 --> 00:57:18.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to cover increased operating needs

asr-000422
00:57:18.880 --> 00:57:20.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and ensure the continuity

asr-000423
00:57:20.000 --> 00:57:21.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of the Bureau's critical programs.

asr-000424
00:57:23.800 --> 00:57:24.900
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: On the other hand,

asr-000425
00:57:24.980 --> 00:57:26.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: following the budget increase

asr-000426
00:57:26.040 --> 00:57:27.060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for building construction

asr-000427
00:57:27.060 --> 00:57:28.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and motor vehicle acquisition

asr-000428
00:57:28.540 --> 00:57:30.280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: under the 2026 GAA,

asr-000429
00:57:30.460 --> 00:57:31.940
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: capital outlays are proposed

asr-000430
00:57:31.940 --> 00:57:34.740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to be 83.2% lower

asr-000431
00:57:34.740 --> 00:57:37.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the 2027 budget.

asr-000432
00:57:38.240 --> 00:57:40.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The BOC's proposed 2027 budget

asr-000433
00:57:40.160 --> 00:57:41.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of 5.9 billion pesos,

asr-000434
00:57:41.820 --> 00:57:42.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: on the other hand,

asr-000435
00:57:42.460 --> 00:57:44.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is 9.7% lower

asr-000436
00:57:44.100 --> 00:57:45.960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: than its 2026 budget.

asr-000437
00:57:46.480 --> 00:57:47.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: A substantial part

asr-000438
00:57:47.400 --> 00:57:48.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of the reduction

asr-000439
00:57:48.000 --> 00:57:49.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is in MOOE,

asr-000440
00:57:49.080 --> 00:57:51.960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: particularly in ICT-related requirements.

asr-000441
00:57:52.200 --> 00:57:53.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our priority is to make full

asr-000442
00:57:53.400 --> 00:57:54.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and effective use

asr-000443
00:57:54.200 --> 00:57:55.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of existing digital systems,

asr-000444
00:57:56.620 --> 00:57:58.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: improve integration across platforms,

asr-000445
00:57:58.840 --> 00:58:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and fund the critical requirements

asr-000446
00:58:00.820 --> 00:58:02.940
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: needed to move modernization forward.

asr-000447
00:58:03.560 --> 00:58:04.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This year-on-year comparison

asr-000448
00:58:04.780 --> 00:58:05.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is also affected

asr-000449
00:58:05.640 --> 00:58:08.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: by the 180.5 million confidential funds

asr-000450
00:58:08.560 --> 00:58:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: specifically provided in the 2026 GAA,

asr-000451
00:58:11.640 --> 00:58:13.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which is no longer included

asr-000452
00:58:13.100 --> 00:58:15.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the 2027 NEP.

asr-000453
00:58:16.600 --> 00:58:18.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Even with a lower budget,

asr-000454
00:58:18.200 --> 00:58:18.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our direction,

asr-000455
00:58:18.780 --> 00:58:19.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: through the BOC,

asr-000456
00:58:19.540 --> 00:58:20.580
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: remains clear and firm,

asr-000457
00:58:20.700 --> 00:58:22.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: faster and more transparent processes,

asr-000458
00:58:22.700 --> 00:58:23.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: better use of technology,

asr-000459
00:58:24.100 --> 00:58:25.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: more effective border administration

asr-000460
00:58:25.880 --> 00:58:26.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and enforcement,

asr-000461
00:58:26.940 --> 00:58:27.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and more efficient

asr-000462
00:58:27.720 --> 00:58:29.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: revenue collection.

asr-000463
00:58:32.400 --> 00:58:33.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Meanwhile,

asr-000464
00:58:33.220 --> 00:58:35.120
